### Provenance & Clearance Note:
The ENABLE (Enhanced North American Benchmark Lexicon) project was established in 1997 specifically to provide software word-game developers with an authoritative, unencumbered, copyright-free alternative to proprietary tournament word lists (such as Hasbro/Merriam-Webster's OSPD). The compilers explicitly released the word list to the **Public Domain**.

### Text Normalization Applied:
- Stripped carriage returns (`\r`) and blank lines.
- Filtered to ASCII alphabetical characters `[A-Z]`.
- Normalized to uppercase.
- Minimum word length enforced by engine: $\ge 2$ characters.

